# Snag (D122, 2026-11-21): the decor kind `snag`, native 28x200, one frame, standing on the floor: a dead tree's trunk
# snapped off 200 px up, for a branch whose tree must stop below the moon (forest-1-mob: a full trunk there crosses the moon
# disc at the room's first camera and breaks the decor ceiling, check_contrast.py). Not solid, never moves; drawn behind the
# play tiles like the trunk. The snapped top (rows 0-5, splinters with a lit edge) is typed; rows 6-199 are the trunk's rows
# 94-287 copied as typed (trunk.grid), so its bark, stub and roots match the trunk's.
# Bark palette as trunk.grid (D130, #555, 2026-11-24: a red-brown pine bark apart from the soil's browns).
size 28 200
color f 220e09
color d 28130e
color m 2e1813
color r 39231d
color l 47302a
color h 454339
color g 1b2416
color k 1c0805
frame snag
